"""Full-budget target-free scrambled Sobol and response-control candidates.

This is an additive successor to the frozen CP1792/RQMC HOLD package.  The CP
host is deliberately absent: in ``A + Q[f - (A + q - E q)]`` its constant
``A`` cancels identically.  What remains is a Hermite-10 mean/covariance host
used only to define the Gaussian linear-response control ``q``.

The two primary classes are a Joe--Kuo Sobol sequence with SciPy-compatible
left-linear-matrix plus digital-shift scrambling, and the same sample bank
with one full-bank empirical whitening transform.  Direction-number metadata
is frozen below; SciPy is neither imported nor required at execution.

Four secondary controlled classes use rank 256 or rank 1024, each with
fixed or cross-fitted beta.  A fifth class is a pure full-budget RQMC control.
Only the final-layer pathwise proxy is evaluated: L1 is exact Gaussian, L2--L15
return the Hermite host, and L16 receives the sampling correction.  This is the
objective-aligned spelling because the official raw target is L16.

``EstimatorRank1024Fixed``
    Uses the fixed coefficient beta=1.
``EstimatorRank1024Crossfit``
    Fits one coefficient per layer and neuron from all *other* shifts, with a
    frozen ridge and clip, then evaluates on the held-out shift.  Conditional
    on the training shifts, beta is independent of the evaluated shift.

The analogous ``EstimatorRank256Fixed`` and ``EstimatorRank256Crossfit`` use
the first 256 normalized Walsh directions.  ``EstimatorRawRQMC`` uses beta=0
and spends no FLOPs on the analytic response.

There is no dataset, target, score, fitted artifact, or network identity in
this source.  Exact unbiasedness applies only to the ideal real-arithmetic,
unclipped randomized-shift law.  The executable clips the inverse-normal tail
and rounds samples to float32; no exact-unbiasedness claim is made for that
executed law.
"""

